# Ledger 127 (ground that is dug under is weighed): a cap of earth on a stem of earth, the stem blasted through; what the
# blast leaves with nothing under it (the stem's stub, the cap over it) comes down.
# Fixed: passes. BS_GROUNDWEIGH=0 (no weighing, as before): the stub and the cap hang in the air and it fails.
# Ledger 216: the cap's outer ring (3 to 5 out: earth corbels one cell) comes down too; BS_OLDWEIGHSPARE=1 (before) it
# hung on in the air and the ring's expects fail.
#   questcheck --scene quest/scenes/crater-settle.scene --headset
at 14 150 14
fly on
load 3
ground -7 120 -7 7 175 7 air
ground -1 40 -1 1 159 1 dirt       # the stem, from deep in the land
ground -5 160 -5 5 162 5 dirt      # the cap
expect ground 0 161 0 == true
blast 0 154 0 4
tick 3
expect ground 0 154 0 == false     # the blast's own hole
expect ground 0 157 0 == false     # the stem's stub over it came down
expect ground 0 161 0 == false     # and the cap's middle over that
expect ground 4 161 4 == false     # ledger 216: the cap's outer ring too
expect ground -4 161 -4 == false
expect ground 5 160 0 == false
expect ground 0 148 0 == true      # the stem under the hole stands
dump -5 150 0 5 163 0
print fps
